      "section": "opening",
      "slot": "opening",
      "text": "Aspose.Cells FOSS for Python provides a free, open-source Python library for creating, reading, and manipulating Excel files in the .xlsx format. It enables developers to work with worksheets, cells, styles, data validation, charts, and encryption without requiring Microsoft Excel or a commercial license. Users can apply formatting via the Style and Font classes, enforce data rules with DataValidation, and protect workbooks using password-based encryption through xlsx_encryptor and decrypt_xlsx. The library supports exporting to .csv and other formats, making it suitable for data processing, reporting, and automation tasks in Python environments."
    },
    {
      "fact_ids": [
