      "section": "scope_limitations",
      "slot": "scope",
      "text": "Aspose.Cells FOSS for Python provides a free, open-source library for working with Excel files in Python, supporting the .xlsx format for loading and saving workbooks, with additional export capabilities for CSV, JSON, and Markdown, and includes a basic formula evaluator for cells without cached values."
    },
    {
      "fact_ids": [
        "format:input.xlsx",
        "format:output.xlsx",
        "inherited_unit:048.list"
      ],
      "section": "scope_limitations",
      "slot": "limitation:1",
      "text": "Only .xlsx is supported for native load and save operations, while CSV, JSON, and Markdown are additional text-format export targets (CSV also supports import), not general spreadsheet formats."
    },
    {
      "fact_ids": [
        "inherited_unit:048.list",
        "public_symbol:aspose.cells_foss.standardencryptionparameters"
      ],
      "section": "scope_limitations",
      "slot": "limitation:2",
      "text": "Only Agile encryption (ECMA-376 Part 2, Section 4) is supported for reading and writing password-protected workbooks; Standard encryption (Section 3) is not yet supported for reading, and the aspose.cells_foss.StandardEncryptionParameters class is not available for use."
    },
    {
      "fact_ids": [
        "inherited_unit:048.list",
        "public_symbol:aspose.cells_foss.formula_evaluator"
      ],
      "section": "scope_limitations",
      "slot": "limitation:3",
      "text": "The aspose.cells_foss.formula_evaluator module provides a basic evaluator for cells without cached values and is not a full spreadsheet calculation engine."
